<title>USA: Ameritech sees $165 mln from sale of shares.</title>
<headline>Ameritech sees $165 mln from sale of shares.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ameritech Corp said it expects to receive cash proceeds of about $165 million in 1997 from the sale of shares of Telecom Corp of New Zealand Ltd, which is carrying out a share repurchase program.</p>
<p>In Ameritech's 1996 annual report, the company said the sale will not materially change its stake in New Zealand Telecom. As New Zealand Telecom is buying back shares, the total number of shares outstanding will decrease.</p>
<p>Ameritech and Bell Atlantic Corp each own a 24.8 percent interest in the company. Ameritech said the value of New Zealand Telecom shares has more than tripled since 1990.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
